---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Editorial Standards & Ethics Policy | Hollywood Time"
  description="Our code of ethics, fact-checking processes, corrections policy, source attribution guidelines, and journalistic integrity standards."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-8">
    <nav class="text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-black">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-900 font-bold">Editorial Standards</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="border-b-2 border-zinc-950 pb-6 mb-10">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-red-600 block mb-2">Ethics & Integrity</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black font-headline tracking-tight uppercase text-zinc-950">
        Editorial Standards & Ethics
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg font-serif text-zinc-600 mt-3 leading-relaxed">
        Hollywood Time operates under strict journalistic principles designed to deliver accurate, fair, and reliable news to global readers.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-zinc-800 font-sans leading-relaxed space-y-8">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">1. Verification and Fact-Checking</h2>
        <p>
          Accuracy is the foundation of Hollywood Time. All news reports, exclusive scoops, and investigative pieces undergo rigorous verification before publication. Reporters are required to verify factual claims with multiple independent sources or corroborated documentation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Quotes, financial figures, release dates, and box office tallies are cross-referenced with primary filings, studio representatives, and official guild records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">2. Corrections & Clarifications Policy</h2>
        <p>
          Hollywood Time promptly corrects errors of fact. When a significant error occurs, the article is updated and a clear editor's note is appended detailing what was changed and why.
        </p>
        <p>
          Readers who spot potential factual discrepancies are encouraged to notify our standards editor immediately at <a href="mailto:corrections@hollywoodtime.com" class="text-red-600 underline">corrections@hollywoodtime.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">3. Anonymous and Confidential Sources</h2>
        <p>
          In entertainment and business reporting, sensitive information often requires protecting source identity. Hollywood Time allows confidential sourcing only when:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>The information is vital to the public interest or industry transparency.</li>
          <li>The source has direct, firsthand knowledge of the matter.</li>
          <li>The information cannot reasonably be obtained on the record.</li>
          <li>The reporter's editor is informed of the source's true identity.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">4. Conflicts of Interest & Studio Relations</h2>
        <p>
          Editorial staff members are prohibited from accepting gifts, fees, or preferential treatment that could compromise journalistic objectivity. Press screenings, review copies, and festival access are utilized strictly for critical review purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any commercial relationship or sponsored feature on Hollywood Time is unambiguously demarcated with prominent "SPONSORED" or "ADVERTISING" labeling.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">5. Originality & Plagiarism Policy</h2>
        <p>
          Hollywood Time enforces a zero-tolerance policy regarding plagiarism. All published commentary, critical reviews, and investigative reporting must be completely original. When citing or crediting exclusive reporting from peer trade outlets, explicit attribution and direct hyperlinks are always provided.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
